cff-version: 1.2.0
title: mitoforge
message: >-
  If you use this pipeline, please cite it as below, and cite the tools it wraps.
  They are listed in CITATIONS.md and at
  https://rcac-bioinformatics.github.io/mitoforge/citations/
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Arun
    family-names: Seetharam
    affiliation: Rosen Center for Advanced Computing, Purdue University
repository-code: "https://github.com/rcac-bioinformatics/mitoforge"
url: "https://rcac-bioinformatics.github.io/mitoforge/"
abstract: >-
  A Nextflow pipeline that assembles, circularises and annotates animal
  mitochondrial genomes from PacBio HiFi or Illumina paired-end reads, for many
  samples at once. HiFi samples are assembled with MitoHiFi and Illumina samples
  with GetOrganelle; every assembly then goes through the same finishing step, so
  all samples get identical outputs.
keywords:
  - nextflow
  - mitochondrial genome
  - mitogenome
  - genome assembly
  - annotation
  - pacbio hifi
  - illumina
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-22"
